//! Parity of `LCEMGP` (the Unity project's contextual models) and of
//! `Interval` constraints with BoTorch (fixtures in
//! `tests/fixtures/unity_lcemgp/*.json`, generated by
//! `scripts/generate_fixtures.py --phase unity-lcemgp`).
//!
//! Every model case is one of the Unity project's LCE-M GPs on BoTorch
//! (`learned` embeddings, `provided` embeddings with a context-specific
//! weight, and `stock`, learned plus fixed embeddings) with K = 2, 3, 5
//! contexts, some without data, m = 1, 3 fixed embedding dimensions and
//! d = 1, ..., 4 inputs:
//!
//! * the optimizer's parameter names, sizes and bounds and the default raw
//!   parameters (exact);
//! * MLL values (1e-9, relative) and gradients (1e-8, relative to the
//!   largest component) at the default and at random raw parameters, and
//!   the in-place renormalization of the embedding weights by a forward
//!   pass (exact);
//! * the constant means of unobserved contexts after `eval()` (exact up to
//!   rounding) and posteriors over the output task (with and without
//!   observation noise), over all tasks and at inputs with a task column,
//!   and the gradient of a weighted sum of the posterior mean and covariance
//!   with respect to the inputs (1e-9);
//! * `fit_gpytorch_mll` from the default parameters, compared with BoTorch's
//!   outcomes: its own fit, the fit with the optimizer's variables reversed
//!   and the fits of twins whose training inputs are perturbed at 1e-14 ..
//!   1e-11 (long L-BFGS-B runs on these likelihoods end in other optima under
//!   rounding-level changes, in either library). botorch_rs fits the same
//!   twins, compared in two stages (`common::compare_fits`, as in
//!   `kernels_6a_parity.rs`; the fixtures record no attempts, all fits
//!   count): on 16 twins, its best final loss must reach BoTorch's best,
//!   and none of its fits may end above BoTorch's worst outcome, both within
//!   max(1e-6, 10 × the spread of BoTorch's outcomes at its best optimum);
//!   if not, statistically on 64 twins;
//! * qLogNEI and qLogNEHVI (on a list with a second model) with BoTorch's
//!   recorded base samples: per candidate set, the nearest of BoTorch's
//!   outcomes on the model and its 16 twins in the regime botorch_rs's value
//!   falls into (on nearly singular posteriors BoTorch's result jumps between
//!   regimes, depending on whether a Cholesky factorization needs jitter);
//!   values 1e-9 (log values absolute below 1) and gradients 1e-8, or 10 ×
//!   the median spread of that regime, whichever is larger.
//!
//! `interval.json`: `Interval` values, inverses, derivatives, raw initial
//! values and optimizer bounds (1e-15), and `SingleTaskGP`s with `Interval`
//! constraints on the lengthscales, the outputscale and the noise (MLL
//! values and gradients, fits with the same tolerance). Run with `--nocapture` to print the error
//! tables.

mod common;

